#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game"
msgstr "Permainan CHSH"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"Contoh terakhir yang akan dibincangkan dalam pelajaran ini bukan satu protokol, tetapi sebuah *permainan* yang dikenali sebagai\n"
"*permainan CHSH*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila kita menyebut permainan dalam konteks ini, kita bukan merujuk kepada sesuatu yang dimainkan untuk hiburan atau sukan, tetapi satu abstraksi matematik dalam erti kata *teori permainan*.\n"
"Abstraksi matematik bagi permainan dikaji dalam bidang ekonomi dan sains komputer, sebagai contoh, dan ia amat menarik serta berguna.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Huruf CHSH merujuk kepada nama pengarang-pengarang — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, dan Richard Holt — sebuah makalah tahun 1969 di mana contoh ini pertama kali diterangkan.\n"
"Mereka tidak menerangkannya sebagai permainan, tetapi sebagai eksperimen.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, penghuraiannya sebagai permainan adalah semula jadi dan intuitif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan CHSH termasuk dalam kelas permainan yang dikenali sebagai *permainan tak setempat*.\n"
"Permainan tak setempat amat menarik dan mempunyai kaitan yang mendalam dengan fizik, sains komputer, dan matematik — menyimpan misteri yang masih belum terpecahkan.\n"
"Kita akan mulakan bahagian ini dengan menerangkan apa itu permainan tak setempat, kemudian kita akan menumpukan perhatian pada permainan CHSH dan apa yang menjadikannya menarik.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Permainan tak setempat {#nonlocal-games}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan tak setempat ialah sebuah *permainan kerjasama* di mana dua pemain, Alice dan Bob, bekerjasama untuk mencapai hasil tertentu.\n"
"Permainan ini dikendalikan oleh seorang *pengadil*, yang bertindak mengikut garis panduan ketat yang diketahui oleh Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob boleh bersedia untuk permainan sesuka hati, tetapi sebaik sahaja permainan bermula mereka *dilarang berkomunikasi*.\n"
"Kita boleh bayangkan permainan ini berlaku di sebuah kemudahan selamat — seolah-olah pengadil berperanan sebagai siasatan dan Alice serta Bob adalah suspek yang disoal siasat di bilik berlainan.\n"
"Tetapi cara lain untuk memikirkan susunan ini ialah Alice dan Bob terpisah oleh jarak yang sangat jauh, dan komunikasi dilarang kerana kelajuan cahaya tidak membenarkannya dalam tempoh permainan berlangsung.\n"
"Maksudnya, jika Alice cuba menghantar mesej kepada Bob, permainan sudah tamat sebelum Bob menerimanya, dan begitu juga sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks each of Alice and Bob a question.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara permainan tak setempat berfungsi ialah pengadil pertama sekali mengemukakan soalan kepada Alice dan Bob masing-masing.\n"
"Kita akan gunakan huruf $x$ untuk merujuk kepada soalan Alice dan $y$ untuk soalan Bob.\n"
"Di sini kita menganggap $x$ dan $y$ sebagai keadaan klasik, dan dalam permainan CHSH $x$ dan $y$ adalah bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengadil menggunakan *kerawakan* untuk memilih soalan-soalan ini.\n"
"Lebih tepat lagi, terdapat kebarangkalian $p(x,y)$ yang dikaitkan dengan setiap pasangan soalan $(x,y)$ yang mungkin, dan pengadil telah berjanji untuk memilih soalan secara rawak, pada masa permainan, mengikut cara ini.\n"
"Semua orang, termasuk Alice dan Bob, mengetahui kebarangkalian ini — tetapi tiada siapa yang tahu khususnya pasangan $(x,y)$ mana yang akan dipilih sehingga permainan bermula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b.$\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah Alice dan Bob menerima soalan mereka, mereka perlu memberikan jawapan: jawapan Alice ialah $a$ dan jawapan Bob ialah $b.$\n"
"Sekali lagi, ini adalah keadaan klasik secara umum, dan bit dalam permainan CHSH.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini pengadil membuat keputusan: Alice dan Bob sama ada *menang* atau *kalah* bergantung pada sama ada pasangan jawapan $(a,b)$ dianggap betul untuk pasangan soalan $(x,y)$ mengikut satu set peraturan tetap.\n"
"Peraturan yang berbeza bermakna permainan yang berbeza, dan peraturan untuk permainan CHSH secara khusus diterangkan dalam bahagian berikutnya.\n"
"Seperti yang telah dicadangkan, peraturan diketahui oleh semua orang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the "
"interactions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rajah berikut memberikan representasi grafik bagi interaksi-interaksi "
"tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Permainan tak setempat](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically "
"the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that "
"makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding "
"suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketidakpastian tentang soalan yang akan ditanya, dan khususnya fakta bahawa "
"setiap pemain tidak tahu soalan pemain lain, itulah yang menjadikan "
"permainan tak setempat mencabar bagi Alice dan Bob — sama seperti suspek "
"yang bersubahat di bilik berlainan cuba menyelaraskan cerita mereka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Huraian tepat bagi pengadil mentakrifkan satu instance permainan tak setempat.\n"
"Ini merangkumi spesifikasi kebarangkalian $p(x,y)$ bagi setiap pasangan soalan bersama peraturan\n"
"yang menentukan sama ada setiap pasangan jawapan $(a,b)$ menang atau kalah bagi setiap pasangan soalan $(x,y).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"It's extremely interesting, in fact, and there are some nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the mind-blowing nature of the non-local games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan melihat permainan CHSH sebentar lagi, tetapi sebelum itu mari kita akui secara ringkas bahawa adalah menarik juga untuk mempertimbangkan permainan tak setempat yang lain.\n"
"Ia memang sangat menarik, malah terdapat beberapa permainan tak setempat yang setakat ini masih tidak diketahui seberapa baik Alice dan Bob boleh bermain menggunakan keterjalingan.\n"
"Susunannya mudah, tetapi terdapat kerumitan yang tersembunyi — dan bagi sesetengah permainan, adalah amat sukar untuk mengira strategi terbaik atau hampir terbaik bagi Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Inilah sifat yang menakjubkan bagi model permainan tak setempat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Huraian permainan CHSH {#chsh-game-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is "
"Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is "
"Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah huraian tepat bagi permainan CHSH, di mana (seperti di atas) "
"$x$ ialah soalan Alice, $y$ ialah soalan Bob, $a$ ialah jawapan Alice, dan "
"$b$ ialah jawapan Bob:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
msgstr "Soalan dan jawapan semuanya ialah bit: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, "
"each of the four possibilities, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(1,1),$ is "
"selected with probability $1/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengadil memilih soalan $(x,y)$ *secara seragam rawak*. Iaitu, setiap "
"daripada empat kemungkinan, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ dan $(1,1),$ dipilih "
"dengan kebarangkalian $1/4.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by"
" listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each "
"pair of questions $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawapan $(a,b)$ *menang* untuk soalan $(x,y)$ jika $a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$"
" dan *kalah* sebaliknya. Jadual berikut menyatakan peraturan ini dengan "
"menyenaraikan syarat menang dan kalah pada jawapan $(a,b)$ bagi setiap "
"pasangan soalan $(x,y).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr "Had strategi klasik {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning "
"with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita pertimbangkan strategi untuk Alice dan Bob dalam "
"permainan CHSH, bermula dengan strategi *klasik*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Strategi deterministik {#deterministic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0,$ and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mulakan dengan strategi *deterministik*, di mana jawapan Alice $a$ adalah satu fungsi daripada soalan $x$ yang diterimanya, dan begitu juga jawapan Bob $b$ adalah satu fungsi daripada soalan $y$ yang diterimanya.\n"
"Jadi, sebagai contoh, kita boleh tulis $a(0)$ untuk mewakili jawapan Alice apabila soalannya ialah $0,$ dan $a(1)$ untuk mewakili jawapan Alice apabila soalannya ialah $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to reason this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered back in the first lesson of the course — so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tiada strategi deterministik yang boleh memenangi permainan CHSH setiap masa.\n"
"Satu cara untuk membuktikan ini ialah dengan memeriksa satu persatu semua strategi deterministik yang mungkin dan memastikan setiap satunya kalah untuk sekurang-kurangnya satu daripada empat pasangan soalan yang mungkin.\n"
"Alice dan Bob masing-masing boleh memilih daripada empat fungsi yang mungkin dari satu bit kepada satu bit — yang kita temui dalam pelajaran pertama kursus ini — jadi terdapat $16$ strategi deterministik yang berbeza untuk diperiksa kesemuanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1),$ then $a(0) = b(1);$ and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga boleh membuktikan ini secara analitik.\n"
"Jika strategi Alice dan Bob menang apabila $(x,y) = (0,0),$ maka mestilah $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"jika strategi mereka menang apabila $(x,y) = (0,1),$ maka $a(0) = b(1);$ dan begitu juga,\n"
"jika strategi menang untuk $(x,y)=(1,0)$ maka $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Jadi, jika strategi mereka menang untuk ketiga-tiga kemungkinan itu, maka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1),$ for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bermakna strategi tersebut kalah dalam kes terakhir $(x,y) = (1,1),$ kerana menang di sini memerlukan\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Oleh itu, tidak ada strategi deterministik yang menang setiap masa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, adalah mudah untuk mencari strategi deterministik yang menang dalam tiga daripada empat kes, seperti $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"Daripada ini kita simpulkan bahawa kebarangkalian maksimum bagi Alice dan Bob untuk menang menggunakan strategi deterministik ialah $3/4.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Strategi kebarangkalian {#probabilistic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang baru kita simpulkan, Alice dan Bob tidak boleh melakukan lebih baik daripada memenangi permainan CHSH 75% daripada masa menggunakan strategi deterministik.\n"
"Tetapi bagaimana pula dengan strategi kebarangkalian?\n"
"Bolehkah kerawakan membantu Alice dan Bob — termasuk kemungkinan *kerawakan dikongsi*, di mana pilihan rawak mereka adalah berkorelasi?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ternyata strategi kebarangkalian tidak membantu langsung untuk meningkatkan kebarangkalian Alice dan Bob menang.\n"
"Ini kerana setiap strategi kebarangkalian boleh dilihat secara alternatif sebagai pemilihan rawak strategi deterministik, sama seperti operasi kebarangkalian boleh dilihat sebagai pemilihan rawak operasi deterministik.\n"
"Purata tidak pernah lebih besar daripada maksimum, dan oleh itu strategi kebarangkalian tidak memberikan sebarang kelebihan dari segi kebarangkalian menang keseluruhan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do "
"using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu, menang dengan kebarangkalian $3/4$ adalah yang terbaik yang boleh "
"dilakukan oleh Alice dan Bob menggunakan sebarang strategi klasik, sama ada "
"deterministik atau kebarangkalian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Strategi permainan CHSH {#chsh-game-strategy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Soalan semula jadi yang perlu ditanya pada ketika ini ialah sama ada Alice dan Bob boleh melakukan lebih baik menggunakan strategi *kuantum*.\n"
"Khususnya, jika mereka berkongsi keadaan kuantum yang terjalin seperti yang dicadangkan oleh rajah berikut, yang boleh mereka sediakan sebelum bermain, bolehkah mereka meningkatkan kebarangkalian menang?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Permainan tak setempat dengan "
"keterjalingan](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawapannya ya, dan inilah inti utama contoh ini dan sebab mengapa ia begitu menarik.\n"
"Jadi mari kita lihat dengan tepat bagaimana Alice dan Bob boleh berbuat lebih baik dalam permainan ini menggunakan keterjalingan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Vektor dan matriks yang diperlukan {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perkara pertama yang perlu kita lakukan ialah mentakrifkan vektor keadaan qubit $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ bagi setiap nombor nyata\n"
"$\\theta$ (yang kita anggap sebagai sudut diukur dalam radian) seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah beberapa contoh mudah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga mempunyai contoh-contoh berikut, yang timbul dalam analisis di "
"bawah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two "
"of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan melihat bentuk umum, kita dapati bahawa hasil darab dalam antara "
"mana-mana dua vektor ini mempunyai formula ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara terperinci, hanya terdapat entri nombor nyata dalam vektor-vektor ini, jadi tiada konjugat kompleks yang perlu dirisaukan:\n"
"hasil darab dalam ialah hasil darab kosinus ditambah hasil darab sinus.\n"
"Menggunakan salah satu *formula penambahan sudut* daripada trigonometri menghasilkan penyederhanaan di atas.\n"
"Formula ini mendedahkan interpretasi geometri bagi hasil darab dalam antara vektor unit nyata sebagai kosinus sudut di antara mereka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these "
"vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar "
"expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita mengira hasil darab dalam antara *hasil darab tensor* mana-mana "
"dua vektor ini dengan keadaan $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle,$ kita memperoleh "
"ungkapan yang serupa, kecuali ia mempunyai $\\sqrt{2}$ di penyebut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but"
" for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kepentingan kita terhadap hasil darab dalam khusus ini akan menjadi jelas "
"tidak lama lagi, tetapi buat masa ini kita hanya memerhati ini sebagai satu "
"formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, takrifkan matriks uniter $U_{\\theta}$ bagi setiap sudut "
"$\\theta$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara intuitif, matriks ini mengubah $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ menjadi $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ menjadi $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Untuk memastikan bahawa ini adalah matriks uniter, pemerhatian utama ialah vektor $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ adalah ortogon bagi setiap sudut $\\theta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, kita dapati bahawa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menulis matriks ini secara eksplisit sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah contoh *matriks putaran*, dan khususnya ia memutar vektor dua dimensi dengan entri nombor nyata sebanyak sudut $-\\theta$ mengelilingi asalan.\n"
"Jika kita mengikut konvensyen standard untuk penamaan dan parameteran putaran dalam pelbagai bentuk, kita ada\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Huraian strategi {#strategy-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "Kini kita boleh menerangkan strategi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a "
"qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the two "
"qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Persediaan:** Alice dan Bob memulakan permainan dengan berkongsi satu "
"e-bit: Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$"
" dan bersama-sama dua qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan"
" $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Tindakan Alice:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question $x=0,$ she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Alice menerima soalan $x=0,$ dia menerapkan $U_{0}$ pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question  $x=1,$ she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit"
" $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Alice menerima soalan $x=1,$ dia menerapkan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Operasi yang Alice lakukan pada $\\mathsf{A}$ boleh diterangkan secara alternatif seperti ini:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Selepas Alice menerapkan operasi ini, dia mengukur $\\mathsf{A}$ dengan "
"pengukuran asas piawai dan menetapkan jawapannya $a$ sebagai hasil ukuran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Tindakan Bob:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=0,$ he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Bob menerima soalan $y=0,$ dia menerapkan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=1,$ he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Bob menerima soalan $y=1,$ dia menerapkan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Seperti yang kita lakukan untuk Alice, kita boleh menyatakan operasi Bob pada $\\mathsf{B}$ seperti ini:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Selepas Bob menerapkan operasi ini, dia mengukur $\\mathsf{B}$ dengan "
"pengukuran asas piawai dan menetapkan jawapannya $b$ sebagai hasil ukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr "Berikut ialah rajah litar kuantum yang menerangkan strategi ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Litar permainan CHSH](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1,$ which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam rajah ini kita melihat dua get terkawal biasa, satu untuk $U_{-\\pi/8}$ di atas dan satu untuk $U_{\\pi/4}$ di bawah.\n"
"Kita juga mempunyai dua get yang kelihatan seperti get terkawal, satu untuk $U_{\\pi/8}$ di atas dan satu untuk $U_{0}$ di bawah, kecuali bulatan yang mewakili kawalan tidak diisi.\n"
"Ini menandakan jenis get terkawal yang berbeza di mana get dilaksanakan jika kawalan ditetapkan kepada $0$ (bukannya $1$ seperti get terkawal biasa).\n"
"Jadi, secara efektifnya, Bob melaksanakan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya jika $y=0$ dan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ jika $y=1;$\n"
"dan Alice melaksanakan $U_0$ pada qubitnya jika $x=0$ dan $U_{\\pi/4}$ jika $x=1,$ yang konsisten dengan huraian protokol dalam perkataan di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to figure out how well this strategy for Alice and Bob works.\n"
"We'll do this by going through the four possible question pairs individually.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini tinggal untuk mengetahui seberapa baik strategi ini bagi Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Kita akan melakukan ini dengan melalui empat pasangan soalan yang mungkin secara individu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case-by-case analysis {#case-by-case-analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis kes demi kes {#case-by-case-analysis}"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"
msgstr "Kes 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kes ini Alice melaksanakan $U_{0}$ pada qubitnya dan Bob "
"melaksanakan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya, jadi keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ selepas mereka melaksanakan operasi mereka "
"ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities for the four possible answer pairs $(a,b)$ are "
"therefore as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kebarangkalian bagi empat pasangan jawapan $(a,b)$ yang mungkin adalah "
"seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can then obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita kemudian boleh mendapatkan kebarangkalian bahawa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq "
"b$ dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan soalan $(0,0),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ dan oleh "
"itu mereka menang dalam kes ini dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"
msgstr "Kes 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kes ini Alice melaksanakan $U_{0}$ pada qubitnya dan Bob "
"melaksanakan $U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya, jadi keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ selepas mereka melaksanakan operasi mereka "
"ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Again, we can obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Sekali lagi, kita boleh mendapatkan kebarangkalian bahawa $a=b$ dan "
"$a\\neq b$ dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan soalan $(0,1),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ dan oleh "
"itu mereka menang dalam kes ini dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"
msgstr "Kes 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kes ini Alice melaksanakan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada qubitnya dan Bob "
"melaksanakan $U_{\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya, jadi keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ selepas mereka melaksanakan operasi mereka "
"ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We find, once again, that probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ are as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita dapati, sekali lagi, bahawa kebarangkalian bahawa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq "
"b$ adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ so they win in"
" this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan soalan $(1,0),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a=b,$ jadi "
"mereka menang dalam kes ini dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"
msgstr "Kes 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The last case is a little bit different, as we might expect because the "
"winning condition is different in this case. When $x$ and $y$ are both $1,$ "
"Alice and Bob win when $a$ and $b$ are *different*. In this case Alice "
"performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so"
" the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform "
"their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kes terakhir ini sedikit berbeza, seperti yang kita jangkakan kerana "
"syarat menang adalah berbeza dalam kes ini. Apabila $x$ dan $y$ kedua-duanya"
" ialah $1,$ Alice dan Bob menang apabila $a$ dan $b$ adalah *berbeza*. Dalam"
" kes ini Alice melaksanakan $U_{\\pi/4}$ pada qubitnya dan Bob melaksanakan "
"$U_{-\\pi/8}$ pada qubitnya, jadi keadaan dua qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ selepas mereka melaksanakan operasi mereka "
"ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities have effectively swapped places from in the three other cases.\n"
"   We obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kebarangkalian-kebarangkalian ini secara efektifnya telah bertukar tempat berbanding tiga kes yang lain.\n"
"   Kita mendapatkan kebarangkalian bahawa $a=b$ dan $a\\neq b$ dengan menjumlahkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(1,1),$ Alice and Bob win if $a\\neq b,$ and "
"therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk pasangan soalan $(1,1),$ Alice dan Bob menang jika $a\\neq b,$ dan "
"oleh itu mereka menang dalam kes ini dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "They win in every case with the same probability:\n"
msgstr "Mereka menang dalam setiap kes dengan kebarangkalian yang sama:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is therefore the probability that they win overall.\n"
"That's significantly better than any classical strategy can do for this game; classical strategies have winning probability bounded by $3/4.$ And that makes this a very interesting example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilah oleh itu kebarangkalian mereka menang secara keseluruhan.\n"
"Itu jauh lebih baik daripada sebarang strategi klasik yang boleh dilakukan untuk permainan ini; strategi klasik mempunyai kebarangkalian menang yang dibatasi oleh $3/4.$ Dan itulah yang menjadikan ini contoh yang sangat menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This happens to be the *optimal* winning probability for quantum strategies.\n"
"That is, we can't do any better than this, no matter what entangled state or measurements we choose.\n"
"This fact is known as *Tsirelson's inequality*, named for Boris Tsirelson who first proved it — and who first described the CHSH experiment as a game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini kebetulannya adalah kebarangkalian menang *optimum* untuk strategi kuantum.\n"
"Iaitu, kita tidak boleh melakukan lebih baik daripada ini, walau apa jua keadaan terjalin atau pengukuran yang kita pilih.\n"
"Fakta ini dikenali sebagai *ketaksamaan Tsirelson*, dinamakan sempena Boris Tsirelson yang pertama kali membuktikannya — dan yang pertama kali menerangkan eksperimen CHSH sebagai sebuah permainan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Gambaran geometri {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is possible to think about the strategy described above geometrically, "
"which may be helpful for understanding the relationships among the various "
"angles chosen for Alice and Bob's operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Adalah mungkin untuk memikirkan strategi yang diterangkan di atas secara "
"geometri, yang mungkin berguna untuk memahami hubungan antara pelbagai sudut"
" yang dipilih untuk operasi Alice dan Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Alice effectively does is to choose an angle $\\alpha,$ depending on her question $x,$ and then to apply $U_{\\alpha}$ to her qubit and measure.\n"
"Similarly, Bob chooses an angle $\\beta,$ depending on $y,$ and then he applies $U_{\\beta}$ to his qubit and measures.\n"
"We've chosen $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa yang Alice lakukan secara efektifnya ialah memilih sudut $\\alpha,$ bergantung pada soalannya $x,$ kemudian menerapkan $U_{\\alpha}$ pada qubitnya dan mengukur.\n"
"Begitu juga, Bob memilih sudut $\\beta,$ bergantung pada $y,$ kemudian dia menerapkan $U_{\\beta}$ pada qubitnya dan mengukur.\n"
"Kita telah memilih $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the moment, though, let's take $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ to be arbitrary.\n"
"By choosing $\\alpha,$ Alice effectively defines an orthonormal basis of vectors that looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Buat masa ini, bagaimanapun, mari kita ambil $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ sebagai sewenang-wenangnya.\n"
"Dengan memilih $\\alpha,$ Alice secara efektifnya mentakrifkan asas ortonormal vektor yang kelihatan seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas untuk Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob does likewise, except that his angle is $\\beta$:\n"
msgstr "Bob melakukan perkara yang sama, kecuali sudutnya ialah $\\beta$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas untuk Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The colors of the vectors correspond to Alice and Bob's answers: blue for "
"$0$ and red for $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Warna vektor sepadan dengan jawapan Alice dan Bob: biru untuk $0$ dan merah "
"untuk $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now, if we combine together $(1)$ and $(2)$ we get the formula\n"
msgstr "Sekarang, jika kita gabungkan $(1)$ dan $(2)$ kita mendapat formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which works for all real numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta.$\n"
msgstr "yang berlaku untuk semua nombor nyata $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following the same sort of analysis that we went through above, but with "
"$\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ being variables, we find this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengikut jenis analisis yang sama yang kita lalui di atas, tetapi dengan "
"$\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ sebagai pemboleh ubah, kita dapati ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude these two formulas:\n"
msgstr "Kita simpulkan dua formula ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These equations can be connected to the figures above by imagining that we superimpose the bases chosen by Alice and Bob.\n"
"In particular, when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = \\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Persamaan-persamaan ini boleh dikaitkan dengan rajah-rajah di atas dengan membayangkan bahawa kita menindih asas yang dipilih oleh Alice dan Bob.\n"
"Khususnya, apabila $(x,y) = (0,0),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = 0$ dan $\\beta = \\pi/8,$ dan dengan menindih asas mereka kita mendapat rajah ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas Alice dan Bob kes 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is $\\pi/8,$ which is the same as the angle between the two blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut antara vektor merah ialah $\\pi/8,$ yang sama dengan sudut antara dua vektor biru.\n"
"Kebarangkalian bahawa hasil ukuran Alice dan Bob bersetuju ialah kosinus-kuasa-dua bagi sudut ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "while the probability they disagree is the sine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"manakala kebarangkalian mereka tidak bersetuju ialah sinus-kuasa-dua bagi "
"sudut ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila $(x,y) = (0,1),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = 0$ dan $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8,$ dan dengan menindih asas mereka kita mendapat rajah ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas Alice dan Bob kes 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy01.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is again $\\pi/8,$ as is the angle between the blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is again the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"Sudut antara vektor merah sekali lagi ialah $\\pi/8,$ begitu juga sudut antara vektor biru.\n"
"Kebarangkalian bahawa hasil ukuran Alice dan Bob bersetuju sekali lagi ialah kosinus-kuasa-dua bagi sudut ini,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"\\pi/8,$ and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila $(x,y) = (1,0),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ dan "
"$\\beta = \\pi/8,$ dan dengan menindih asas mereka kita mendapat rajah "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas Alice dan Bob kes 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy10.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bases have changed but the angles haven't — once again the angle between vectors of the same color is $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is\n"
msgstr ""
"Asas-asas telah berubah tetapi sudut-sudutnya tidak — sekali lagi sudut antara vektor dengan warna yang sama ialah $\\pi/8.$\n"
"Kebarangkalian bahawa hasil ukuran Alice dan Bob bersetuju ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the probability they disagree is\n"
msgstr "dan kebarangkalian mereka tidak bersetuju ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ and $\\beta = "
"-\\pi/8.$ When we superimpose their bases, we see that something different "
"has happened:\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila $(x,y) = (1,1),$ Alice dan Bob memilih $\\alpha = \\pi/4$ dan "
"$\\beta = -\\pi/8.$ Apabila kita menindih asas mereka, kita nampak sesuatu "
"yang berbeza telah berlaku:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Asas Alice dan Bob kes 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/strategy11.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the way the angles were chosen, this time the angle between vectors having the same color is $3\\pi/8$ rather than $\\pi/8.$\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is still the cosine-squared of this angle, but this time the value is\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan cara sudut-sudut dipilih, kali ini sudut antara vektor yang mempunyai warna yang sama ialah $3\\pi/8$ bukannya $\\pi/8.$\n"
"Kebarangkalian bahawa hasil ukuran Alice dan Bob bersetuju masih merupakan kosinus-kuasa-dua bagi sudut ini, tetapi kali ini nilainya ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability the outcomes disagree is the sine-squared of this angle, "
"which in this case is this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kebarangkalian hasil ukuran tidak bersetuju ialah sinus-kuasa-dua bagi sudut"
" ini, yang dalam kes ini adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remarks {#remarks}"
msgstr "Catatan {#remarks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic idea of an experiment like the CHSH game, where entanglement leads to statistical results that are inconsistent with purely classical reasoning, is due to John Bell, the namesake of the Bell states.\n"
"For this reason, people often refer to experiments of this sort as *Bell tests*.\n"
"Sometimes people also refer to *Bell's theorem*, which can be formulated in different ways — but the essence of it is that quantum mechanics is not compatible with so-called *local hidden variable theories*.\n"
"The CHSH game is a particularly clean and simple example of a Bell test, and can be viewed as a proof, or demonstration, of Bell's theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Idea asas bagi eksperimen seperti permainan CHSH, di mana keterjalingan menghasilkan keputusan statistik yang tidak konsisten dengan penaakulan semata-mata klasik, adalah berasal dari John Bell, penama bagi keadaan-keadaan Bell.\n"
"Atas sebab ini, orang ramai sering merujuk kepada eksperimen seperti ini sebagai *ujian Bell*.\n"
"Kadangkala orang juga merujuk kepada *teorem Bell*, yang boleh diformulasikan dalam pelbagai cara — tetapi intipatinya ialah mekanik kuantum tidak serasi dengan apa yang dipanggil *teori pemboleh ubah tersembunyi setempat*.\n"
"Permainan CHSH adalah contoh ujian Bell yang sangat bersih dan mudah, dan boleh dilihat sebagai bukti, atau demonstrasi, teorem Bell.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game offers a way to experimentally test the theory of quantum information.\n"
"Experiments can be performed that implement the CHSH game, and test the sorts of strategies based on entanglement described above.\n"
"This provides us with a high degree of confidence that entanglement is real — and unlike the sometimes vague or poetic ways that we come up with to explain entanglement, the CHSH game gives us a concrete and testable way to *observe* entanglement.\n"
"The 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics acknowledges the importance of this line of work: the prize was awarded to Alain Aspect, John Clauser (the C in CHSH) and Anton Zeilinger for observing entanglement through Bell tests on entangled photons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Permainan CHSH menawarkan cara untuk menguji teori maklumat kuantum secara eksperimental.\n"
"Eksperimen boleh dilakukan yang melaksanakan permainan CHSH, dan menguji jenis strategi berasaskan keterjalingan yang diterangkan di atas.\n"
"Ini memberikan kita tahap keyakinan yang tinggi bahawa keterjalingan adalah nyata — dan tidak seperti cara yang kadangkala kabur atau puitis yang kita hasilkan untuk menerangkan keterjalingan, permainan CHSH memberikan kita cara yang konkrit dan boleh diuji untuk *memerhati* keterjalingan.\n"
"Hadiah Nobel Fizik 2022 mengakui kepentingan bidang kerja ini: hadiah tersebut diberikan kepada Alain Aspect, John Clauser (C dalam CHSH) dan Anton Zeilinger kerana memerhati keterjalingan melalui ujian Bell pada foton yang terjalin.\n"
